          "exact": "ENIAC (//; Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer)[1][2] was the first programmable, electronic, general-purpose digital computer, completed in 1945.[3][4] Other computers had some of these features, but ENIAC was the first to have them all. ENIAC was Turing-complete and able to solve \"a large class of numerical problems\" through reprogramming.[5][6]\nENIAC was designed by John Mauchly and J."
